      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "STUDY OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the frequency and range of appendiceal disease in women with endometriosis and right lower quadrant (RLQ) pain, and to estimate the value of preoperative gastrograffin enema (GGE) as a screen for the disease."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "DESIGN",
          "content": "Nonrandomized clinical trial (Canadian Task Force classification II-2)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "SETTING",
          "content": "University-affiliated hospital with a private practice setting."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "PATIENTS",
          "content": "A subpopulation of 65 women from a group of 337 patients undergoing laparoscopy for symptomatic endometriosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "INTERVENTION",
          "content": "Preoperative GGE was performed whenever possible in these women. At laparoscopy, the appendix was removed if it appeared abnormal or if the preoperative GGE was positive."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "MEASUREMENTS AND MAIN RESULTS",
          "content": "Of 65 women (19%) with symptomatic endometriosis and preoperative RLQ pain, 52 (80%) underwent appendectomy as part of surgery. Of these 52 excised appendixes, 39 (75%) had histologically confirmed pathology including appendicitis or periappendicitis, endometriosis, fibrous obliteration, lymphoid hyperplasia, and carcinoid tumor. Preoperative GGE had sensitivity of 74% and specificity of 83% for appendiceal disease. Its positive predictive value was 95% and negative predictive value was 42%. No complications from laparoscopic appendectomy occurred."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "Disease of the appendix is common in women with endometriosis and RLQ pain. Appendectomy is particularly likely if preoperative GGE is positive."
        }
      ]},
